{
  "name": "tread",
  "//": "TREADING WATER: the body upright and still at the surface (Space held, no direction). Hands scull in front at chest height, sweeping in and out twice a cycle with the palms turning into each sweep; the legs egg-beater, each thigh up and out and the shins circling half a cycle apart. A slow bob on the hips. Rotations: hips = lean Z (+ = right) of pitch X (+ = forward) of roll Y; every other part = sweep Y of flex X of abduction Z. A hanging limb: X negative = forward/up, positive = back; Z negative = the RIGHT limb out from the side. Knees +X bend, elbows -X bend. Hips pos in decimetres. All six swim clips share one 1200 ms period and one playhead (pose.cpp, the swim family), so a blend of two directions strokes in step.",
